<v Mike Hall>I'm a firm believer in listening to creators, which is why we're here, and yeah I agree. Even if you're a Clojure person and you have a chance to hear somebody who created a language and framework as ubiquitous as PHP, you need to listen.

00:07:32.896 --> 00:07:45.196
<v Eric Kingery>Yeah, absolutely, and technologies change so fast that even if you're on the cutting edge of say PHP, you might have missed server-side JavaScript, functional languages, or advances the Ruby and Python communities have made.

00:07:45.196 --> 00:07:49.973
