00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:19.186
<v Eric Kingery>Yeah, exactly. They teach a lot of valuable things, but the software engineering environment is so complex that a lot of things are missed. Unless you have a good mentor or work for a company that espouses professional practices, you can miss those things.

00:08:19.186 --> 00:08:23.688
<v Mike Hall>Right, university classes don't cover a lot of these practical engineering skills.

00:08:23.688 --> 00:08:43.071
<v Eric Kingery>Yeah, unit testing, continuous integration, HTTP basics, API design, software process. A lot of these things are thrown out there as a professional developer, and unless you go to conferences like SCNA it can be difficult to pick those up. So we want to expand beyond PHP and talk about how to develop software in a professional environment effectively.

00:08:43.071 --> 00:08:45.762
<v Mike Hall>Bringing that refactoring concept to your career.

00:08:45.762 --> 00:08:57.238
