00:08:57.238 --> 00:09:00.148
<v Mike Hall>Yep, yeah, so bringing that refactoring concept to...

00:09:00.148 --> 00:09:33.204
<v Eric Kingery>So refactoring your career overall, exactly. Everything. So depth from full stack, you know, full stack from the way you think about approaching problems to what tools are now in your arsenal. For sure, because you're missing something if you're laser-focused. In some professions and careers you can go really deep, and we want to learn from those people as well. But most people I've found in the software profession benefit more from having wide exposure, and you need that to operate in an ecosystem as diverse as most software engineering teams in small, mid-range, and large companies these days.

